   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Existence and location: hay vs. está",
     "texto": [
      "Use **hay** to state that something exists or is available, often with indefinite articles: *Hay una farmacia aquí*, *Hay dos bancos*.\n\nUse **está** to pinpoint the location of a specific, known person or object: *La farmacia está al lado del banco*.\n\n**Hay** remains unchanged for singular and plural nouns.\n\nWith **al lado de**, de + el obligatorily contracts to **del**: *al lado del banco*."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Using hay and estar",
     "texto": [
      "Compare:\n- **Hay** una farmacia en la plaza (states that one exists).\n- La farmacia **está** al lado del banco (locates that specific pharmacy)."
     ],
     "ejemplos": [
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       "estudio": "Hay una farmacia en la plaza.",
       "alumno": "There is a pharmacy in the square.",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [
        [
         "Hay una farmacia en la plaza",
         "predicate"
        ],
        [
         "Hay",
         "verb head"
        ],
